# vTual — channels, content, ingestion

- **Canonical content is not multi-owned.** One `vtual_contents` row per `(platform_id, external_id)`; `channel_id`/`creator_id` = the **primary host** (API truth, single `snippet.channelId`). Extra channels are **appearances** (`vtual_content_appearances`, role `primary|collaborator|network`). Never write "owned by multiple channels" / "multi-owner content". Auto-detecting appearances from platform HTTP is **cancelled by design** (no safe signal) — attach is explicit.
- **Channel** is unique per `(platform_id, external_id)` with `visibility` `public|private`. Public profile, feed poll and WebSub include `public` only; Discord discovery may bind private rows until the owner promotes.
- **Channel add is dual-path:** an actual owner/editor **member** (`memberRoleFor`, not the staff `roleFor` override) starts a **claim** + bio token; staff (`manage any`) on an orphan stores `profile_input` as a **pending** row (placeholder `external_id=pending:{uuid}`) resolved later by the registration flush. Pending rows are **force-deleted**, never archived (422 `channel.pending_not_archivable`).
- **Pools** (non-interactive, per platform, one `Cache::lock` + claim-to-`processing` so a set is never fetched twice): fetch pool flush at ≥50 pending unique ids or 15 min; registration pool same gate; `claim_verify_pool` for bio verify (Accept Anyway stays sync). Commands `vtual:flush-channel-pool` (registration phase **first**), `vtual:flush-claim-verify-pool`; scheduled every minute, hourly `--resync` for stale/null `last_synced_at` or null `subscriber_count`.
- **Hydrate vs stub:** `hydrated_at` null = stub (archived-channel feed/WebSub ingest, no API quota); set on full API hydrate. `status=unavailable` + `first_unavailable_at` = tombstone (WebSub `at:deleted-entry` or `videos.list` omission); a successful hydrate clears it. Public profile/directory hide archived-primary-channel rows **and** unavailable rows.
- **Onboarding** = `ChannelActivationService` (WebSub subscribe + `RunChannelInitialContentBackfillJob` together). Feed poll skips channels until `content_initial_backfill_at` is set; the backfill seeds `feed_last_entry_updated_at` from the persist watermark (no second Atom call). Legacy repair: `vtual:backfill-initial-content`, `vtual:renew-websub-subscriptions --repair-missing`.
- **Flow:** feed/WebSub discovery (0 quota) → content pool (`videos.list` batch ≤50) → `ChannelContentFetchService::fetchVideosAndPersist` → `ContentService::upsertFromPrimary`. WebSub and feed share one pool; upsert is idempotent.
- **Archive/restore:** archive keeps WebSub + feed poll **alive** but ingests stubs only (no hydrate, live poll, or refresh); restore resubscribes WebSub and runs the stub backfill. Both are rate-limited (429, `channel.lifecycle_*`).
- **WebSub hardening:** GET verify accepts only `hub.mode` subscribe/unsubscribe and marks verified only from an allowed state (unknown mode → 403, no challenge echo); POST dual HMAC (`sha1=`/`sha256=`, hex or base64), body cap `vtual.websub.max_body_bytes` (413), invalid signature → 204 + log + `last_error`. Topic lookup by exact `topic`, then `channel_id` parsed from the topic URL. Twitch EventSub mirrors this with one row per channel × event type (`channel.update`, `stream.online`, `stream.offline`), signed verification flipping `pending|failed → active`, and a graceful skip when no active credential exists.
- **Classification layer 1** `content_type` (`music|non_music|null`) is program-only and deterministic in `ContentKindClassifier` — **not** `categoryId` alone: topic → categoryId → title/uploader-tag keyword (never the description) → original credit + link → long-form (`long_form_min_seconds`) → null (unknown, left for the AI audit). `topicDetails` **must stay** in `config('vtual.youtube.default_video_parts')` or the layer silently degrades. Twitch → null.
- **Classification layer 2** `content_category` (`cover|original|singing_stream|null`) + `content_category_detail` runs inline during hydrate, recomputed every hydrate (idempotent), never throws. Decision order: original title label → singing stream → strong cover label → composer credit → uploader tags → provenance (`本家`/`原曲` + music link) → weak cover + corroboration → iTunes catalog artist test. Strip cover-**art** credits before matching; the English word `original` is **not** a provenance marker; vocabulary stays narrow (`feat.`, `acoustic`, bare `歌` were removed as false positives).
- **AI audit** may set **either** layer for rows the program pass left unknown; where the program pass produced a verdict that verdict stays authoritative. Never throws — failure/malformed JSON/low confidence returns null and leaves the row untouched; negative verdicts are cached so the pool does not re-ask. `max_tokens` must cover reasoning tokens (default 4000, floor 256) or the reply arrives empty with `finish_reason: length`. Endpoint/key come from the Ai domain via the Tier B slug `vtual.content_classification.ai.connection`; the rest is Tier B (`vtual.content_classification.ai.*`).
- **Audit plumbing:** hydrate enqueues a pending row in `vtual_content_ai_audit`; `vtual:audit-content-ai` (scheduled every 5 min, `--limit=5`, `withoutOverlapping`) drains it — without the drainer the table is write-only. `attempts` is charged at claim time; `--stale-minutes` returns killed rows to pending. Backfill `vtual:classify-contents` never overwrites an existing verdict; use `--refresh` after a classifier change (pair with `--ai`, because the queue is only fed on hydrate). Stored rows carry no `categoryId`/`topicCategories`/`tags`.
- **Region restriction** is a **notice, never a filter**: `region_allowed`/`region_blocked` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, empty normalized to null) are read at hydrate, exposed on every content payload, and the card renders a notice — restricted rows stay listed everywhere. Twitch stays null. It is not an entitlement check.
- **Live predicate lives in one place:** `Support\LiveContentScope` (non-archived channel, live row as primary host **or** appearance) — directory cards, profile `is_live`, landing live strip and management roster must not re-derive it.
- **Public API:** no auth, no `domain.access`, no `product.active`; throttled 60/min; slug-addressed; **never** exposes claim tokens, `claim_process_url`, `blocked_until`, or UUIDs. Unknown filter values **clamp to the default, never 422**; `sort=oldest` drops live-first pinning; a profile 404s unless the creator is active with ≥1 active+public channel.
- **Landing payload** is forever-cached (`PublicLandingCache`, key `vtual.public.landing`) and must be flushed on Content/Creator/Channel/**VtualEvent** writes and on `vtual.landing.*` settings upsert. `vtual.landing.*` is Tier B read via `setting()`.
- **Platform credentials:** envelope-encrypted `secret_payload` (+ system-owned `runtime_payload`, never from a FormRequest), HMAC fingerprint, mask-only API — **never** return payloads, tokens, or fingerprint. Any edit resets to `pending` and clears `runtime_payload`/`verified_at` (re-Test required); `active` must be revoked before delete. `pickActive()` skips soft-demoted and never selects `pending`. Workers must go through `PlatformCredentialService` so invalidate paths stay consistent. Kick stays `enabled=false` until an official API decision.

- **History is append-only and best-effort.** `Support\VtualMetricRecorder` appends bucketed samples (`insertOrIgnore` on `(subject, bucket_start)`, so a burst inside one bucket collapses to one row; a null metric writes nothing rather than shadowing the bucket) and `Support\VtualContentStatusRecorder` appends **transitions only** — a content row *is* a session, its `external_id` is the platform stream session id, so a six-hour stream polled every 2 minutes leaves two rows. Both write from a seam that already holds a fresh value (activation, pool flush, claim verify, hydrate, end-of-stream, tombstone) and **never throw**: a metric write must not fail the hydrate that carries it. Pruned by `vtual:prune-metrics` on `vtual.metrics.retention_days` (default 90). Decision: [reference-metrics.md](../../docs/domains/vtual/reference-metrics.md).

